      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T18:52:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like a workaround for a crash in an HCI timeout situation (which causes a crash) I\u0027d rather not add logic for this.",
      "revId": "bb7b532c17da613c2aef16ef5b6fd38bd2179dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8eac5af0_9aa26e18",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1966830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T19:07:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is a workaround. But it is to avoid crashes due to vendor specific commands which are not expecting command status. This CL does not add logic. It just adds another command status `COMMAND_DISALLOWED` in addition to UNKNOWN_HCI_COMMAND. I have to rewrite the code to add a flag. From the previous CL which added the logic, it creates an empty Command Complete such that it will be interpreted by the command-complete-handler as invalid.",
      "parentUuid": "9fbee1cb_b08ed14a",
      "revId": "bb7b532c17da613c2aef16ef5b6fd38bd2179dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
